    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0463" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/1–2352: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1952-01-23T19:21:00+01:00">January 23,
                            1952—7:21 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Gadel 813. Re Membership: Dept was seriously concerned re letter Guidotti
                    considered sending other SC members as reported
                        Delga 1128,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d322-f1"
                    /> since letter wld have given distorted impression re our position. <pb
                        facs="0464" n="442" xml:id="pg442"/> However, in view recent developments
                        (Delga 1148 and 1149), we assume Guidotti
                    now has no intention send such letter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
